@Pinks_on_pink @AC__3_3 @kd03281512323 @niccruzpatane @grok What nonsense, my Model Y has 45K miles and original tires are just fine.

EVs weight is more evenly distributed, which helps reduce tire wear. Similar class ICE vehicles and EVs have similar curb weights. 

The only thing affecting tire wear is driving style and EVs instant torque. Young aggressive drivers may burn though tires more easily on an EV. If you don’t race at every stoplight your tires will last.

@ns123abc A 2T valuation never made sense to me. Compared to SpaceX, Anthropic has no other product lines other than the model itself. Their ARR revenue acceleration was while but they were the first to produce a model that was useful for coding with a decent lead ahead of others. At this point they are still the leader in coding ability if not by much. Other models can do 95% of the tasks as much less cost and open source models have gotten very good as well. Companies are also turning to open source on prem in order to not give Anthropic their proprietary data. That 2T valuation was justified due to the ARR acceleration would continue but I don’t see that continuing at the same rate. They will still continue to be in the frontier but that is diversifying across multiple models. 

Additionally I believe this is why they are pushing for regulation. Possibly under pressure from their investors.

SpaceX has Data centers and ability to stand up compute faster than anyone, Leader in reusable Rockets and capacity by many years, X platform, Starlink which is growing faster than any competitor by far, Solar production ramp, Grok, Cursor, and eventually Terafab. All these show real revenue trajectory justifying the valuation.
